                <p class="bolderFont">
                    This November, Vilpa Films will unveil its latest innovation at the Dubai International Content
                    Market 2026.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Its name is <span class="bolderFont">Vilpa Oracle.</span>
                </p>
                <p>
                    Built at the intersection of film, data and artificial intelligence, Vilpa Oracle is a new
                    intelligence
                    layer designed to help producers understand a film before they make it.
                </p>
                <p>
                    For decades, some of the most consequential decisions in filmmaking have been made using information
                    that exists everywhere — but rarely in one place.
                </p>
                <p>
                    A screenplay tells one part of the story. A budget tells another. Production requirements,
                    historical performance, comparable films and financial variables tell others.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The producer is expected to connect them all.
                </p>
                <p class="bolderFont">The Oracle is being built to do something new: understand the relationships
                    between them.
                </p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Introducing Vilpa Oracle</h5>
                <p>Oracle transforms the creative, physical and financial characteristics of a film production into
                    decision intelligence.</p>
                <p>By analyzing a project against historical film data, Oracle identifies relevant comparables,
                    strengths, critical vulnerabilities and relationships between production decisions that might
                    otherwise remain hidden. It brings together information traditionally scattered across creative,
                    production and financial workflows into a single intelligence layer.</p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">You'll meet Lucien</h5>
                <p>At the center of Oracle is Lucien, an AI assistant that makes this intelligence conversational.
                    Instead of navigating complex analytics, producers can ask questions, explore vulnerabilities,
                    understand comparables and interrogate The Oracle's findings through natural conversation.</p>
                <p class="bolderFont">Oracle provides the intelligence. Lucien makes it accessible.</p>
                <p>This is where production intelligence meets a new generation of generative AI. The first wave showed
                    us what AI could create — text, images, music and video. The Oracle explores what comes next: AI
                    that
                    helps us understand.</p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont">Dubai International Content Market</h5>
                <p>Vilpa Oracle will be unveiled publicly for the first time at Dubai International Content Market 2026,
                    alongside the market debut of Blue Shades, Vilpa Films' upcoming original animated series.</p>
                <p>There is a small crossover between the two: Lucien was originally conceived as a character within the
                    <span class="bolderFont">Blue Shades</span>
                    universe before becoming the AI assistant behind The Oracle — bringing one of Vilpa Films'
                    fictional IPs into its real-world technology ecosystem.</p>
                <p>The unveiling marks Vilpa Films' expansion beyond producing and distributing entertainment and into
                    technology built specifically for the industry it operates in.</p>
